{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And HaShem afflicted Pharaoh.</b> Scripture did not specify the plagues of Pharaoh, unlike the plagues of Avimelech which it did specify — because immediately after the episode of Avimelech it is written, 'And HaShem remembered Sarah'; therefore it explained that the plagues came upon him because he had taken her, so that they would not be able to say: Avimelech fathered Yitzhak. But the episode of Pharaoh is before the remembering of Sarah; therefore it did not bother to mention the plagues. And if you ask: why was he punished — did Avraham not say 'she is my sister,' as it is written, 'Why did you say she is my sister'? One may explain <b>because of the matter of Sarai the wife of Avram</b> — 'because of the matter of Sarai the wife of Avram am I.' And furthermore, there is no warning for a descendant of Noach, as we say further on regarding Avimelech." "<b>And HaShem afflicted Pharaoh.</b> Rashi: he was afflicted with the plague of ra'atan, so that relations were painful for him. Measure for measure — and likewise regarding Avimelech: 'For HaShem had completely restrained every womb in the house of Avimelech.' Rabbi Levi taught in the name of Rabbi Abba: we heard regarding Pharaoh that he was afflicted with tzara'at, and Avimelech was restrained — from where do we apply what is stated of this one to that one? Scripture says <b>on account of</b> — for a gezeirah shavah."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:04.266681721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}